      <p>The egress router implementation uses the egress router Container Network Interface (CNI) plugin.</p>
      <h2 id="nw-egress-router-ovn-cr_deploying-egress-router-ovn-redirection" class="group scroll-mt-20">Egress router custom resource<a href="#nw-egress-router-ovn-cr_deploying-egress-router-ovn-redirection" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can define the configuration for an egress router pod in an egress router custom resource. </p>
      <p>The following YAML describes the fields for the configuration of an egress router in redirect mode:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: network.operator.openshift.io/v1\nkind: EgressRouter\nmetadata:\n  name: <egress_router_name>\n  namespace: <namespace>\nspec:\n  addresses: [\n    {\n      ip: \"<egress_router>\",\n      gateway: \"<egress_gateway>\"\n    }\n  ]\n  mode: Redirect\n  redirect: {\n    redirectRules: [\n      {\n        destinationIP: \"<egress_destination>\",\n        port: <egress_router_port>,\n        targetPort: <target_port>,\n        protocol: <network_protocol>\n      },\n      ...\n    ],\n    fallbackIP: \"<egress_destination>\"\n  }"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where:</p>
